What are Petroleum Based Agricultural Spray Oils?
Petroleum based agricultural spray oils are specialized formulations derived from highly refined petroleum fractions, serving dual roles as either stand-alone pesticides or performance-enhancing adjuvants for herbicides and insecticides. These oils are categorized by viscosity - with low-viscosity variants preferred for foliar applications on delicate crops and high-viscosity oils used in dormant season applications. Modern formulations include emulsifiable concentrates and crop oil concentrates designed for compatibility with various spraying systems while minimizing phytotoxicity risks.

The market's trajectory reflects agriculture's shifting paradigms. As growers worldwide grapple with pesticide resistance and environmental regulations, petroleum-based oils offer a strategic middle ground between traditional chemicals and newer biological alternatives. Their ability to smother pests physically while enhancing chemical efficacy makes them particularly valuable in high-value horticultural sectors like orchards and vineyards.

